> 00:00:54.816\nShe could not. But ultimately,\n\n00:00:54.817 --> 00:00:56.376\nthis is on her record forever.\n\n00:00:56.377 --> 00:00:57.576\nLike, and sometimes,\n\n00:00:57.577 --> 00:00:59.936\nyou guys, social media is not the first place you should run to.\n\n00:00:59.937 --> 00:01:01.856\nMaybe talk to a lawyer, maybe talk to an adult,\n\n00:01:01.857 --> 00:01:03.616\nmaybe talk To. I don't care.\n\n00:01:03.617 --> 00:01:06.296\nSomebody that can give you information about how to move forward.\n\n00:01:06.297 --> 00:01:08.576\nI don't think she thought it was gonna go the way it ended up going.\n\n00:01:08.577 --> 00:01:10.356\nBut this is just a lesson to everyone.\n\n00:01:10.656 --> 00:01:12.536\nSocial media is not always the answer.\n\n00:01:12.537 --> 00:01:15.336\nPosting the things that happen to you is not always the answer.\n\n00:01:15.337 --> 00:01:16.296\nPlease, please,\n\n00:01:16.297 --> 00:01:18.336\nplease. Always find out what's the rules.\n\n00:01:18.337 --> 00:01:19.576\nFind out what's illegal.\n\n00:01:19.577 --> 00:01:22.956\nWas that man right to have his pants around his knees when he,\n\n00:01:23.057 --> 00:01:26.636\nor Doordash person was coming to deliver his food and have his door wide open?\n\n00:01:26.776 --> 00:01:30.536\nNo. Was she right to take the video and post it on social media?\n\n00:01:30.537 --> 00:01:33.536\nNo. Was there another way to handle the situation?\n\n00:01:33.537 --> 00:01:35.536\nYes. And that's all I'm saying.\n\n00:01:35.537 --> 00:01:38.496\nJust another lesson. Social media is a real thing.\n\n00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:39.696\nI know we say, uh,\n\n00:01:39.697 --> 00:01:41.736\nsocial media is not real, but it's a real thing,\n\n00:01:41.737 --> 00:01:44.016\nit's a real place, and it has real consequences.\n\n00:01:44.017 --> 00:01:45.976\nSo just keep that in mind when you guys are posting\n"
