rges.\n\n00:01:03.781 --> 00:01:05.060\nIf he has ring camera footage\n\n00:01:05.061 --> 00:01:08.400\nof her physically pushing the door open and walking inside,\n\n00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.220\nthat is actually breaking and entering.\n\n00:01:10.221 --> 00:01:11.380\nAnd we would have seen that charge,\n\n00:01:11.381 --> 00:01:15.020\nbut we're not. Both of those charges have To do with that video footage\n\n00:01:15.021 --> 00:01:18.760\nand her intent in taking that video footage to post it online\n\n00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.580\nso she had something to talk about.\n\n00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:23.780\nAnd at the same time completely invading his privacy,\n\n00:01:23.781 --> 00:01:27.100\nreleasing his house number as well as him in a vulnerable,\n\n00:01:27.101 --> 00:01:28.420\nnaked position. No,\n\n00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.120\nI'm not saying that ring camera footage doesn't exist.\n\n00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.660\nAnd if it does, when she goes back to court on December 4th,\n\n00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.940\nwe may see that additional charges have been added\n\n00:01:36.941 --> 00:01:40.740\nif that footage does show that she unlawfully entered the residence\n\n00:01:40.741 --> 00:01:42.920\nor unlawfully pushed the door open.\n\n00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.380\nBut the one thing that I will say is\n\n00:01:44.381 --> 00:01:47.400\nthere is a lot of rumours going around about this situation,\n\n00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:51.160\nand the best thing to do is to stick to the evidence that we've seen,\n\n00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:55.900\nwhich is the fact that she took video of him while he was passed out and naked,\n\n00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:58.772\nand she posted it online to profit off her TikTok account.\n"
