        "transcript": "WEBVTT\n\n\n00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.460\nOlivia Henderson, aka the Influencer Doordash Girl,\n\n00:00:03.461 --> 00:00:07.201\nhas just been arrested. She's facing two felony charges,\n\n00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:09.500\none for distributing surveillance footage\n\n00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.721\nand another for illegal surveillance.\n\n00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.900\nHonestly, this isn't surprising at all.\n\n00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:17.501\nThink about it. You can't secretly film someone in their home,\n\n00:00:17.502 --> 00:00:19.581\nupload the videos online for profit,\n\n00:00:19.582 --> 00:00:21.341\nreveal their name and address,\n\n00:00:21.342 --> 00:00:23.541\nand then expect there to be no consequences.\n\n00:00:23.542 --> 00:00:28.861\nThe law isn't optional. This is the most basic line you don't cross.\n\n00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:31.981\nReports say she was officially arrested on October 10.\n\n00:00:31.982 --> 00:00:35.381\nDistributing surveillance footage means publishing private recordings\n\n00:00:35.382 --> 00:00:38.341\nobtained illegally with the intent to harm,\n\n00:00:38.342 --> 00:00:40.461\nharass or threaten the person involved.\n\n00:00:40.462 --> 00:00:42.701\nIllegal surveillance means filming someone\n\n00:00:42.702 --> 00:00:45.001\nwithout their knowledge or consent\n\n00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.460\nin a place where they have a right to privacy,\n\n00:00:47.461 --> 00:00:51.721\nlike their home. If she had just handed the footage over to the police,\n\n00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.300\nshe might have had some Protection.\n\n00:00:53.301 --> 00:00:55.381\nBut she chose to post it publicly,\n\n00:00:55.382 --> 00:00:56.661\nletting everyone see it,\n\n00:00:56.662 --> 00:00:59.021\nwhich inevitably meant she would face consequences.\n\n00:00:59.022 --> 00:01:00.821\nThis isn't just an online scandal.\n\n00:01:00.822 --> 00:01:03.841\nIt highlights a gray area in modern social media.\n"
